    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d811">

                <pb facs="0956" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg862"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-09-16"><hi rendition="#italic">September 16,
                        1896</hi></date>. (Received Oct. 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 985 B.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In regard to the increased guard demanded
                    for the mission property at Harpoot by the British consul, you are aware, from
                    my former dispatches, that before the recent disturbances here began I had
                    demanded from the Porte a guard for the protection of American life and property
                    which would be ample under all circumstances. I will renew representations at
                    the Porte to insure an immediate compliance with this request. Since writing the
                    above, a letter from Harpoot, inclosed in my 988, informs me that the Sultan
                    had, before the British consul acted, ordered special protection.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
